From f9f0e92c3c3bd76bb84c07d29b0bfa4f6c1871f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Ottenhoff <AlexanderOttenhoff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 03:07:24 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Android build and direct start (--rom, --skip-launcher,
 --game-mode)

- CMake: the game is a shared library on Android; SDL2 found before the
  subprojects; a stub nfd target (no native file dialogs); file_to_c and
  DXC run on the build machine (RT64_HOST_FILE_TO_C, host CPU).
- RT64 presents to the ANativeWindow behind SDL's window, in RGBA8; the
  menu renderer's swap-chain format matches.
- No window icon on Android (__gnu_linux__ only); <sstream> for libc++.
- --rom selects and validates the ROM, --skip-launcher starts the game
  without the launcher; --game-mode is accepted and ignored (this
  runtime has no custom game modes).

Same change as our Mega Man 64: Recompiled patch: both projects are
copies of Zelda64Recomp's dev-branch frontend.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
